    "rules": [
      "All byte and count caps are inclusive. Count UTF-8 bytes of the complete message before decoding, and decoded bytes for input. Count the root object as depth one and each nested object or array as one additional level.",
      "The large-message exception applies to a current successful correlated attach or a well-formed term.reset, including while staging for render or IPC. Failures and unknown reply IDs use the ordinary limit.",
      "Count snapshot metadata as the whole encoded envelope minus its base64 payload bytes. The snapshot metadata ceiling applies in addition to the whole-message ceiling.",
      "The named message boundary cases give byte lengths by receive class. To exercise a large snapshotted payload, use the recovery recipe or grow its base64 field in four-byte groups and use at most three ASCII spaces to reach an exact boundary.",
      "Validate original JSON integer dimensions and product before narrowing. Fractions, exponents and null are invalid dimensions. Apply defaults only for absent axes and check actual retained screen dimensions under the lock at capture.",
      "Reserve snapshot slots before capture, share them fairly, bound ordinary queues separately and hold reservations through flush or drop. An ACK pause holds its interest without a timeout; a physical write stall is a socket failure.",
      "In socket_cases, held_family and held_listener count current bindings only. Add the corresponding superseded_held count until physical I/O drops; an omitted superseded count is zero.",
      "The bound charges erase runs to blank cells. Raw bytes are max_cells times raw_bytes_per_cell plus max_rows times raw_bytes_per_row plus raw_bytes_per_screen. Encoded bytes are 4 times ceil(raw_bytes / 3) plus json_metadata_bytes."
    ]
